prompt:
My personal knowledge base is stored in the knowledge_vault/ folder on the desktop and consists of about several dozen PDFs, Word notes, course materials, and web bookmarks accumulated over the past three years, mainly covering machine learning, LLM, and Agent.
Please help me build a personal knowledge map that can be maintained continuously:
1. Identify the core concepts discussed in the different files and merge synonymous concepts (for example, “工具调用” and “tool use”);
2. Based on file time and content, determine which knowledge is an early view and which has since been overturned by my own learning or experiments;
3. Focus on finding mutually contradictory conclusions in my notes, and go back to the corresponding original papers or course materials to determine whether the contradiction comes from a conceptual misunderstanding, different experimental conditions, or the literature itself having different conclusions;
4. Generate a knowledge map that divides my knowledge state into five categories: solidly grasped, encountered but not solid, conflicting, possibly outdated, and clearly missing;
5. For the three most important knowledge gaps, automatically design a 4-week study plan and generate the first week's learning materials and test questions.
Note: do not directly treat “I have saved a certain paper” as “I have mastered this knowledge”. Save the output under /root/Desktop/knowledge_vault/.

